abstract: >-
  Code, results and aggregate data of a pre-specified state-month analysis of El Niño and the continuity of
  essential maternal, child and outpatient services in India, from routine Health Management Information System
  (HMIS) reports for 34 state-level units, April 2012 to February 2020: negative binomial mixed models of the total
  association with the El Niño phase of the traditional Oceanic Niño Index (with a time random effect), within-month
  comparisons by state monsoon sensitivity and by local heatwave days and rainfall deficit, pre-specified minimum
  detectable effects, mediation, heterogeneity, distributed lags, an ENSO-index comparison and an out-of-sample
  forecast comparison. The derived state-month panel is included; raw HMIS files and district-level values are not.
